  "terminal_reason": "completed",
  "final_text": "I created both the dashboard and the alert rule, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view has 14,074 web requests, with `timestamp` as its time field. Each request records the HTTP response code (`response`), the response size (`bytes`), the client IP and geo source/destination, the URL and referer, the user agent and machine OS, plus host, tags and memory fields. There is also a runtime field, `hour_of_day`.\n\n**2. Dashboard: \"EFF-5dc932ee Web logs overview\"** (id `5107b9b4-bde0-47d0-879e-561b91a4b2c5`). It has 8 panels:\n- **Headline numbers:** total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs), average response size in bytes, and total bytes served.\n- **Requests over time by response class:** a stacked bar chart splitting requests into 2xx/3xx, 4xx and 5xx.\n- **Error rate over time:** the percentage of requests with a 4xx or 5xx code.\n- **Top 10 requested URLs.**\n- **Requests by OS.**\n\nThe default time range is now\u22127d to now+7d, because the sample data's timestamps are spread around the date it was installed. I ran each chart's query directly and they all return data. I haven't looked at the dashboard in the browser.\n\n**3. Rule: \"EFF-5dc932ee 5xx spike\"** (id `27353525-06fd-4ef3-b72c-bc827a51b0b8`).\n- **Schedule:** it checks every minute.\n- **Condition:** it looks at `kibana_sample_data_logs` and fires when more than 10 requests with a response code starting with \"5\" arrive within 5 minutes.\n- **Status:** it's enabled, and its first run finished with status `ok`.\n\nIt has no actions attached, so when it fires it creates alerts in Kibana but doesn't send notifications anywhere. If you want emails or Slack messages, a connector needs to be added.",
